{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558464-v20-ogham-fixing-durations","id":1558464,"title":"[V20] Ogham fixing durations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-02-23T00:15:32-08:00","id":1558464,"title":"[V20] Ogham fixing durations","content":"Looking at the V20 version of Ogham it seems to me like some of the powers have pretty terrible ration when it comes to the time you need to activate them and the time they last, making them basically unusable.<br /> Maybe I'm overlooking something, but here is what I think needs to be fixed.<br /> <br /> The 1st level power seems to only need an action to be activated, so trge duration of 1 scene should be fine.<br /> <br /> The 2nd level power needs one scene to activate and than last only one, considering that this power is only usefull for combat, it is basically unusable. I think it needs to be changed to either one action to activate, or it has to last for an entire night. Not sure what makes more sense.<br /> <br /> The 3rd level option seems to only take an action to activate and last indefinitely if glyph isn't erased. So it should be ok,<br /> <br /> The 4th level power seems also to last indefinitely, so there is also no change needed.<br /> <br /> The 5th level power needs from my understanding also a sceen to activate and than last only a sceene. Concidering all the conditions neccessary to use the powere at all, I think it should last untill all the dice are used up (maybe with some limit on how many dice you can add to a single roll). But Maybe I'm missing how this power is intended to be used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-24T08:51:09-08:00","id":1558489,"title":"","content":"Must admit that i never paid much attention to the specifics of Ogham's write-up in V20.<br /> <br /> In my own games, due to the common themes of territoriality, witchcraft and &quot;kind of but not quite Gangrel vibes&quot; shared between both groups, i tend to just handwave the Lhiannan as a gaelic/celtic branch of the Tzmisce, Ogham as a path of blood magic Keeps things simple while bringing some extra lore complexity/confusion/clashes to the table.<br /> <br /> Or would, if i ever had players asking to play them, that is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My players coterie is at present three Caitiffs - or more precisely, a Caitiff (of Assamite antitribu descent), a fledgling pushed into serving as grunt for the prince that killed his sire, eventually toppled the bastard along with the anarchs, only to very recently discovered its <b><i>Cappadocian</i></b> heritage (through the help of noddist, an anarch elder and a taxi driver <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) and a probable Malk that claims to have been embraced by Dracula - a Salubri warrior-nun recently awakened from torpor, a Gangrel that was turned into a Gargoyle in the middle ages but has been &quot;reset/saved&quot; by, on his words, Caine himself.\u200b And later on, a Toreador poet-historian of good lineage that happens to have an interest in alternate kindred myths unrelated to Caine and &quot;Drowned Legacies&quot; due to his particular connection with native american legendry from his mortal life and a british Assamite cybercafe attendant &amp; hacker that moved into Milwaukee with her sire in the big Banu Haqim exodus.\u200b<br /> <br /> Anyway, and sorry for my digression, no &quot;Lhiannan/Tzim&quot; PCs in my game and just a passing mention as NPC group - that happened to be bretonic, so technically french.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T05:52:54-07:00","id":1561969,"title":"","content":"So, the things you overlooked:<br /> <br /> 2nd level power is a battle prep. The idea is to use for a big skirmish to happen soon, not to use in the fly for any fight. You'll plan an attack or notice enemies approaching, and prepare for that battle.<br /> <br /> Expanding to the whole night may be too much, as it's a heavy Diff reduction for Frenzy, and the other effects will have limited usefulness: the reduced damage penalty will disappear after 4 damage taken, and the enhanced attack is only one.<br /> <br /> This is a cheap preparation to get a useful set for an important ambush. At most what I could suggest is to let the preparation and activation have a hiatus in between, but I wouldn't worry too much. If made to regular use this power would be too much effect for very little cost.<br /> <br /> 5th level is just badly worded. The scene isn't to be immediately before the use. You spend a scene to prepare the place, after that activation is reflexive for as long as the runes are in place and that's it. The limit on draining the Caern or Node is the most pressing matter, as it take a long time to recover. This is not for regular use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-28T23:19:53-07:00","id":1564409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558464-v20-ogham-fixing-durations?p=1561969#post1561969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2nd level power is a battle prep. The idea is to use for a big skirmish to happen soon, not to use in the fly for any fight. You'll plan an attack or notice enemies approaching, and prepare for that battle.</div> </div> </div> </div>But even under these conditions the power only lasting one scene basically means that, in case of skrimish you have to perform the ritual almost right next to your target, and in case of you being attacked, that you have an entire scene to prep.<br /> <br /> How well that will work depends entirely your ST's interpretation of what scene is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558464-v20-ogham-fixing-durations?p=1561969#post1561969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Expanding to the whole night may be too much, as it's a heavy Diff reduction for Frenzy, and the other effects will have limited usefulness: the reduced damage penalty will disappear after 4 damage taken, and the enhanced attack is only one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Form my understanding the whole thing ends once you take 4 damage, and that's why I think increasing the duration wouldn't be a problem, it would just make it easier to use the power for prep without being reliant on the mercy of the ST.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5199,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","user":"Aahz","date":". 09-29-2026, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-29T02:36:36-07:00","id":1564413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558464-v20-ogham-fixing-durations?p=1564409#post1564409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But even under these conditions the power only lasting one scene basically means that, in case of skrimish you have to perform the ritual almost right next to your target, and in case of you being attacked, that you have an entire scene to prep.<br /> <br /> How well that will work depends entirely your ST's interpretation of what scene is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a tactical power. Think of it as something to use before an invasion, or under siege. Both the Discipline and the Bloodline draw heavily from references of Roman battles against the Pictish and Celtics in Britannia.<br /> <br /> That means fights in a context of territorial control: ambushes, sieges, invasions. You hound your target, stay hidden, prepare for the upcoming battle, then fall upon them with your full might. The Pictish in particular were likened to forest ghosts due to their ambushes and fear tactics.<br /> <br /> Used the way it's intended, it gives you a lot of tactical options: you can use the attack bonus to guarantee your first target falls, or rely first on surprise and save it for another target. You can set the place on fire and stay put thanks to the Frenzy bonus. And you can account for any tactic that will risk some damage to yourself.<br /> <br /> As most Bloodline Disciplines it's quite niche, I know. But the problem is that a character build with such tactics in mind can pull them with a considerable consistency. Plan preemptive attacks on rivals, prepare your territory to give you prep time if someone approaches, this is really not hard if it is what you want.<br /> <br /> Lhiannan are made for this style of play. This vampire focus on tending their own territory, it is usually already a hard place to navigate, like a forest, and they'll prepare to defend it and to actively watch nearby threats.<br /> <br /> What's the risk if you change the power to fit another play style? Someone who follows the regular style can find ways to abuse it. I can think a few things I'd try if I had the opportunity that may not be what the ST intended, like using it to become a serial arsonist.<br /> <br /> Crimson Woad has three distinct effects. The strength of it isn't in any of them being much powerful, but the toolbox being very versatile if you plan ahead. Don't think the character have a combat bonus that ends in a few turns taking regular damage. Thinks the character will have a whole night with bonus against Frenzy, plus one super attack to dish at their convenience, plus some extra buffer against damage if this is at all necessary. And Animalism + Presence means they're likely not alone.<br /> <br /> So, I would at least try to run a Lhiannan with a more tactical bent first to see how that works. Careful planning, castle mentality, avoid fair fights. See if expanding the timing of Crimson Woad risks making this too effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-02T04:22:22-07:00","id":1564471,"title":"","content":"Feels like Ogham 2 is missing some delayed activation clause.<br /> <br /> Like the implied thematic seems to be<br /> 1. Dramatic scene, paint weird temporary tattoos over yourself. <br /> 2. Start some foolhardy action sequence.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThere's a dramatic cut between 1 and 2 that's not really accounted for by the v20 description. Time on the bus doesn't count?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-02T05:15:58-07:00","id":1564474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558464-v20-ogham-fixing-durations?p=1564471#post1564471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like the implied thematic seems to be<br /> 1. Dramatic scene, paint weird temporary tattoos over yourself.<br /> 2. Start some foolhardy action sequence.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> It's closer to:<br /> <br /> 1. Find out where the enemy lives.<br /> 2. Go there and spy from some distance.<br /> 3. Dramatic scene.<br /> 4. Start an ambush action sequence.<br /> <br /> The key mistake is that the idea is not a foolhardy action sequence. It was never a foolhardy action sequence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}